hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"275","Ahmad bin Abdah informed us, Hammad bin Zaid informed us. H Ali bin Khashram told us, Ibn Uyaynah told us. H Yahya bin Hakim told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us. H. Salam bin Junada told us, Waki’ told us. H. Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, that Malik told them, all of them, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa. H Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb told us, Abu Usama, Hisham told us. H, and here we are Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Mukhurami, and we are Abu Muawiyah, and we are Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Fatima bint Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abi Bakr, that a woman asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about menstrual blood getting on the clothes, and he said: “Gather it, then sprinkle it with water, then Sacrifice him.” This is the hadith of Hammad, and in the report of Ibn Uyaynah: “Then sprinkle water and pray in it,” and in the report of Yahya: “Then sprinkle it and pray in it,” and he did not mention The others mentioned sprinkling or sprinkling. They only mentioned rubbing and pinching with water, then praying over it, except that in the hadith of Wakee’: Squeeze it, then pinch it with water, Nothing more than this"
